ifa/issues/178 -- two records of one class built with identical argument types, whose member holds an int list for one and a str list for the other, so `self.labels[j]` reads {int64, str} ("expression has mixed basic types"). IFA_DBG_CSDEFSPLIT: while the Pot CreationSet has both creation points, route 4 declines it as "confluence only, no demand" (the demand sits on its member lists), and the owner lift from those lists reaches it but finds one group (`11 11`: both creation points reach both content keys, because the key follows value flow into the member and never the receiver of the store). PYC_RETDEMAND does not reach it (no unresolved dispatch; every rvalue demand finds no actuator). CPython prints `5 4`, which the check file records, so this flips to PASS when the writer split lands.
